STRUCTURAL NOTE (direction; not a proof claim).  The elementary
consequence of the checked squaring law r_{k+1} <= r_k^2 is
    n_k + 2 = ceil(1/r_k) >= x^{-2^k}, hence
    A(N) <= log_2( log(N+2)/log(1/x) ) = O_x(log log N),
an UPPER bound.  A lower bound A(N) = Omega_x(log log N) needs a
positive lower bound on r_{k+1}/r_k^2, which rh41 refutes.  The
register's attribution of Omega_x(log log N) to this same squaring
law therefore appears directionally inverted; the genuinely
open/matching side is the LOWER bound.  Flagged for adjudication.

VERDICT: OP-13 remains OPEN as a two-sided almost-everywhere law.
Finite exact-rational evidence: (i) the elementary upper consequence
of the checked squaring law, A(N) <= log_2 log N + O_x(1), held on
every one of the 100510 pooled takes (0 violations) and the fitted
constant is c = 1.36 < 1/log 2 = 1.4427; (ii) A(N)/log log N has no
positive lower floor (its cross-orbit mean falls from 1.38 to 0.98 as
N grows), consistent with rh41's refutation of a positive lower bound
for r'/r^2; (iii) small ratios obey a power law P(r'/r^2 <= eps) ~
eps^1.11 and run frequencies ~ p_1^L, i.e. no heavy clustering.  This
is finite evidence only — no proof is claimed in either direction.
